  "notes": "Shared by the API (pytest) and the portal (vitest); both parsers must agree on every row. Only ASCII whitespace (space, tab, CR, LF, FF, VT) is trimmed or allowed: a no-break space or any other Unicode space is invalid, so do not use String.trim() as is. The trimmed text is at most 64 characters and the number has at most 9 digits before the decimal point. Minutes are rounded half up on the magnitude, then the sign is applied (-2.5 minutes is -3, where Math.round gives -2). Display picks the singular label when the rounded number shown is exactly 1 and shows no sign when it rounds to 0. Row shapes: parse, lag, parse_alt and parse_default_h are [text, minutes, unit, elapsed]; format, format_lag and format_alt are [minutes, unit, elapsed, text].",
